{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And He chose his seed.</b> A hint to Jacob, for if it said 'in their seed' the seven nations [nations in addition to us?] would enter with us." "<b>And He brought you out before His face.</b> With the anger that He grew angry against Egypt. And some say it is like 'and the angel of His face saved them' [Isaiah 63:9]. And in my opinion it is like 'and Your face goes in our midst' [Exodus 33:15]."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:20.821619217Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}